{ vs the Morra. Because the c-file stays closed in the declined lines, a queen on c7 is comfortable and completely safe - which is not always true in the accepted lines. Move-order psychology: playing ...g6 and ...d6 before ...Bg7 means opponents pre-select their reply against the fianchetto and miss the chance to stop ...Bg4 with h3. } 1. e4 c5 2. d4 cxd4 3. c3 d3 { Decline by returning the pawn rather than accepting. } 4. Bxd3 Nc6 5. Nf3 d6 { Insert ...d6 BEFORE the fianchetto - it lets the c8-bishop come to g4. } 6. O-O g6 7. Re1 Bg4 { Trading the f3-knight reduces White's attacking potential and is the speedrun's practical plan. } 8. Be3 Bg7 9. Nbd2 Nf6 10. h3 Bxf3 11. Nxf3 O-O *

